! mcp_bootstrap_p122.strap -- "RECEPTOR", printed page 122.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.129.  HEADER READ, NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID
! EB000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 122", rendered at
! 600 dpi; the page number field reads a clean "122".
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  Lines 1-3 are a banner of asterisks
! spelling R E C E P T O R -- this page opens the receptor, the
! routine the parallel-interrupt vectors on printed p.113 branch to.
! printed p.112's deck records that MCP's I-O interrupt row names
! "SPSIOI (receptor)" and "KSTORE", and KSTORE is line 5 of THIS
! page at 215710.00: p.112 lines 12-16 all branch to "215710.34 0C
! ... K STORE".  So this is the landing site of those five
! BZB1 vectors, and the five-way test it does on lines 8-15 (BOPZ,
! BUKZ, BEEZ, BZEOPZ, BCSZ) is the same five indicators in the same
! order -- OP, UK, EE, EOP, CS.
!
! Lines 5-48 are forty-four rows of straight code: save the lower
! registers, test the five interrupt indicators, dig the equipment /
! unit / file-area table entries out through index registers 10-14,
! and branch out to K SINGL, K SIGNL, K SPACE, K WEF, K RELAY,
! K NORM, K STACK, K COPY, K GATE and C ARC AD.
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The card-serial column
! runs EB000001 (line 1) .. EB000047 (line 48) with no gap; printed
! p.120 was still punching EA serials.  Forty-eight lines, forty-
! seven cards: lines 27 and 28 ("SIC,K ST CS" and "B,K CS IN") share
! EB000027, the same SIC+B-on-one-card habit p.120 shows at its
! lines 1-2 and 8-9.  Serials were read at 600 dpi at the top (4, 5,
! 6, 7, 8, 9) and the bottom (43, 44, 45, 46, 47), so nothing fell
! off either end of the render.
!
! >>> TAIL SCOPE. <<<  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved
! the origin to 0o215000 and these pages are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G
! block that printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Names here may repeat
! names defined in pp.2-98 at other addresses; that is scope, not a
! collision.  Nothing on this page collided with a landed deck.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN, AND WHAT IT WITNESSES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS "SLC,$", SO ITS LOCATION IS A FREE JOIN
! WITNESS. <<<  Line 4 is
!
!     4*   215707.71  *                      SLC,$
!
! and an SLC emits nothing, so 215707.71 *is* the counter arriving
! from printed p.121 -- printed by IBM's own assembler.  The ".71"
! was read at 1800 dpi and is not ".11" or ".17": 0o71 = bit 57, so
! p.121 leaves the counter 57 bits into word 215707, NOT on a half-
! word boundary.  p.121's last two rows are "48* 215707.00" and
! "49* 215707.40", both "VF,UNDEF", so its final row consumes 25
! bits (0o40 + 25 = 0o71).  When p.121 lands, compare by hand.
!
! This deck writes the printed value as a hard SLC, which ASSERTS
! the origin rather than checking it (docs/transcription_workflow.md
! "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" #2).  It is written as "(8)215707.71"
! because inside an (8) literal BOTH parts are base 8, so the bit
! offset goes in exactly as printed.  It was TESTED, not assumed:
! with this origin line 5's full-word TRANSMIT realigns to the next
! word and lands on the printed 215710.00, and every one of the
! forty-four binary rows and six symbols below passes.
!
! BUT BE PRECISE ABOUT WHAT THAT TEST PINS.  Every origin from
! 215707.41 through 215707.77 realigns to 215710.00 identically, so
! the checks establish only "past the last half-word boundary in
! word 215707".  The exact ".71" rests on the 1800-dpi read of the
! printed SLC location and on nothing the oracle can confirm --
! the same limitation recorded below for the K-symbols.
!
! The page LEAVES the counter at 215746.40 -- line 48 is a half-word
! branch at 215746.00.  The full-volume OCR shows PDF p.130 (printed
! p.123) line 1 as "215746.40 ... K GATE  BZB,S UNSLP($11),..." and
! THIS page's line 44 branches to "215746.74 00", i.e. half-word
! 215746.40 named K GATE.  The forward join is closed from both
! sides without p.123 being transcribed.
!
! CONFIRMED BY THE AGENT WHO TRANSCRIBED printed p.123, from that
! page and not from this one: p.123 line 1 is at 215746.40, p.123's
! header carries "LOCATION 215746", and p.123 DEFINES K GATE at
! 215746.40.  Three readings, no disagreement -- this page's last
! row is the half word at 215746.00 and the counter leaves at
! 215746.40.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * "K DOOL" (line 32).  At 1800 dpi this page prints the third
!   glyph open, so it reads "K DOCL" in isolation.  SETTLED BY A
!   SECOND PRINTING: printed p.124 (PDF p.131) line 49 is
!   "216052.00  215732.10 C0   B,K DOOL" -- a branch to THIS page's
!   215732 -- and there both O's are closed at 1800 dpi.  Dropout
!   opens a closed glyph and never closes an open one, so the
!   closed pair wins.  Name: KDOOL.
! * "C ARC AD" (line 48).  C/D is the pair the workflow doc calls
!   the worst, and nothing landed references this symbol.  Settled
!   the same way: its DEFINING card, printed p.129 (PDF p.136) line
!   14 at 216316.00, prints "C ARC AD" with the straight vertical
!   left stem of a D.  The volume OCR reads "C ARC AC" there and is
!   simply wrong about D.  The "C " prefix is ordinary in this
!   region (C ERROR, C MINTP, C WAIT, C SUPP all print nearby).
! * "S FAKE I" (line 20) and "K KK" (line 29) DO NOT REST ON INK
!   ALONE either -- both are branched to from elsewhere in the
!   volume, so a misspelling here would fail the merge.  The volume
!   OCR carries "216311.40  215721.50 C0  B,S FAKE 1" (half word
!   215721.40 = this page's line 20) and "216053.40  215730.10 00
!   B,K KK" (215730.00 = this page's line 29).  The addresses are
!   the OCR-robust part and both land exactly on this page.
! * "K STORE" (line 5) is independently SYN'd by the landed deck
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p112.strap as "KSTORE SYN,(8)215710.0" --
!   the same spelling at the same address, read off a different
!   page.
! * "K SINGL" (line 22) and "K SIGNL" (line 24) ARE TWO DIFFERENT
!   SYMBOLS, not one misread twice: their printed branch addresses
!   are 216050 and 216054, four words apart, and both are defined
!   on printed p.124.  Read at 1200 dpi: SINGL has no G, SIGNL has
!   one.
! * "$1C" (lines 18 and 29).  Printed with the last glyph open.  It
!   is "$10": line 30 prints a closed "($10)" in the same column,
!   and $10 is index register 10, which lives at word 0o32 = 26 --
!   exactly the address line 18 compiles ("000032.24 B0").  There
!   is no system symbol "$1C".
! * "TI" and not "T1" (lines 5 and 6).  printed p.116's deck quotes
!   this very row in a comment as "T1,13,$UB,S TLR", but T1 is not
!   a STRAP transmit mnemonic (TRANSMIT_CODES has T/TI/TB/TBI and
!   the SWAPs) and this page's glyph has the top and bottom bars of
!   an I, unlike the flagged 1 two characters later in "13".
! * "C0011" (line 38) and "CM0111" (line 10).  The character after
!   the C prints round; a connective's suffix is four binary digits,
!   so it is 0.
! * Lines 11 and 28 print their hex byte as "C0" at 1800 dpi and are
!   "00".  See the note on those two !CHECK rows below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every spelling and value below was taken from a deck that already
! landed, not invented here -- SEQUIP, SUNIT, SMULTI, SSETUP, SCTL,
! SRD, SWR, SUNA from decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap; SIOINS and
! SFIAAC from p101; SCCW from p102; SCHANS from p103; SPSIOI from
! p112 (which settled "S PS IOI" against "SPSICI" from the manuals);
! STLR from p117.  Each one's value is independently confirmed by
! the binary this page prints for it, listed beside it.
!
! >>> THE K-SYMBOLS ARE KNOWN ONLY TO THE HALF WORD. <<<  KSINGL,
! KSIGNL, KSTCS, KCSIN, KNORM, KRELAY, KSPACE, KWEF, KGATE and
! CARCAD are back-derived from printed branches and one LVI.  Bit
! offsets 0 through 31 all encode identically; only bit 32, the
! half-word select, shows.  So ".0" below is a CONVENTION and no
! !CHECK can test it; ".40" where it appears IS observed, because
! that is bit 32.  Two of them were WRONG as ".0" and the oracle
! caught it: K ST CS is at 216272.40 (line 27 prints "216272.40 80")
! and K RELAY is at 216314.40 (line 34's second half prints
! "216314.74 06", whose bit 50 is the half-word select).  The volume
! OCR's own index agrees: "216272.4C ... K ST CS" and "216314.40
! ... K RELAY".

STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! p117; lines 5,6,7,10,23,26 "S TLR"
SPSIOI  SYN, (8)215226.0             ! p112; lines 9,11 print 215226.11/.22
SCHANS  SYN, (8)215002.0             ! p103 (SYN,SXCHAN); line 19 "215002.24"
SEQUIP  SYN(BU,4), 0.52              ! p99 line 38; line 20 prints 000000.64
SUNIT   SYN(BU,3), 0.56              ! p99 line 39; line 29 prints 000000.70
SMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27              ! p99 line 24; line 22 prints 000000.33
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31              ! p99 line 29; line 34 prints 000000.37
SCTL    SYN(BU,1), 0.60              ! p99 line 48; line 42 prints 000000.74
SRD     SYN(BU,1), 0.57              ! p99 line 45; line 43 prints 000000.71
SWR     SYN(BU,1), 0.58              ! p99 line 46; line 44 prints 000000.72
SUNA    SYN(BU,25), 0.0              ! p99 lines 19/20; lines 30,32 print 0
SFIAAC  SYN(BU,18), 3.0              ! p101 line 13; line 33 prints 000003.32
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! p101 line 17; line 40 prints 000004.52
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! p102 line 15; line 45 prints 000004.21

KSINGL  SYN, (8)216050.0             ! line 22 "216050.34 00"  (bit offset unobservable)
KSIGNL  SYN, (8)216054.0             ! line 24 "216054.34 C2"  (bit offset unobservable)
KSTCS   SYN, (8)216272.40            ! line 27 "216272.40 80"  (half word IS observed)
KCSIN   SYN, (8)216267.0             ! line 28 "216267.10 00"  (bit offset unobservable)
KRELAY  SYN, (8)216314.40            ! line 34 "216314.74 06"  (half word IS observed)
KNORM   SYN, (8)215776.0             ! line 35 "215776.03 01"  (bit offset unobservable)
KSPACE  SYN, (8)216204.0             ! line 41 "216204.34 02"  (bit offset unobservable)
KWEF    SYN, (8)216213.0             ! line 42 "216213.34 02"  (bit offset unobservable)
KGATE   SYN, (8)215746.40            ! line 44 "215746.74 00"  (half word IS observed;
                                     !   and it is printed p.123 line 1's own location)
CARCAD  SYN, (8)216316.0             ! line 48 "216316.32 C2"  (bit offset unobservable)

        SLC, (8)215707.71            ! line  4  printed "215707.71 *  SLC,$"

KSTORE  TI,13,$UB,STLR               ! line  5  -SAVE LOWER REGISTERS
        TI,0,$0,STLR+13.0            ! line  6
        BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101    ! line  7  -STM(U),STLR+1.0 - SAVE $MR.
        BOPZ,$.32                    ! line  8  -FOR LASL LRL
        L(BU,5),SPSIOI+.9            ! line  9
        CM0111(BU,5),STLR+8.9        ! line 10
        Z,SPSIOI                     ! line 11
        BUKZ,$+.32                   ! line 12
        BEEZ,$+.32                   ! line 13
        BZEOPZ,$+.32                 ! line 14
        BCSZ,$.32                    ! line 15
        LV,14,$CA                    ! line 16
        LV,10,$CA                    ! line 17
        V+,10,$10                    ! line 18
        V+,10,SCHANS                 ! line 19
SFAKEI  L(BU,4),SEQUIP($10),-19      ! line 20
        LV,4,$L                      ! line 21  -EQUIP CODE IN VF($4)
        BZB,SMULTI($10),KSINGL       ! line 22
        L(BU,4),STLR+8.9,-13         ! line 23
        BRZ,KSIGNL                   ! line 24
        LC,7,$L                      ! line 25
        BZB,STLR+8.13,$+2.           ! line 26
        SIC,KSTCS                    ! line 27
        B,KCSIN                      ! line 28
KKK     L(BU,3),SUNIT($10),-18       ! line 29
        LV,11,SUNA($10)              ! line 30
        V+,11,$L                     ! line 31  -COMPUTE UNIT TABLE ENTRY ADDR
KDOOL   LV,12,SUNA($11)              ! line 32  -OBTAIN UNIT AREA TABLE
        LV,13,SFIAAC($12)            ! line 33  -OBTAIN ACTUATED FILE AREA
        BBZ,SSETUP($11),KRELAY       ! line 34
        LVI,1,KNORM                  ! line 35
        KVI,4,4.0                    ! line 36  -IS EQUIP TAPE
        BZXE,KSTACK                  ! line 37
        C0011(BU,2),$7.37            ! line 38  -TEST IF EPGK OR UK ON
        BZRZ,KSTACK                  ! line 39
        L(BU,8),SIOINS+.42($12)      ! line 40
        BB,$7.39,KSPACE              ! line 41  -IS EE ON
        BB,SCTL($11),KWEF            ! line 42  -IF NOT, CHECK IF WEF OP
KSTACK  BB,SRD($11),KCOPY            ! line 43
        BZB,SWR($11),KGATE           ! line 44
KCOPY   CCW,0.0($14),SCCW($13)       ! line 45
        BEKJZ,$-1.0                  ! line 46
        KVI,4,.32                    ! line 47  -IS EQUIP DISK
        BXE,CARCAD                   ! line 48

