!
! THE ASTERISK IN THE LOCATION COLUMN appears on lines 4, 22 and 39
! (and on line 4 only, after a location with no binary).  Recorded,
! not interpreted; printed p.117's deck already notes one the same
! way.  Nothing in the oracle consumes it.
!
! >>> LINES 11 AND 28 PRINT THEIR HEX BYTE AS AN OPEN "C0" AND ARE
! "00". <<<  At 1800 dpi both bytes show a first glyph broken open
! on the right.  Three independent reasons settle them as 00:
!   (a) WHAT PRODUCED THEM.  Both are format-2 ops -- "Z,S PS IOI"
!       (MISC) and "B,K CS IN" (unconditional branch).  Their 6-bit
!       literal at bits 22-27 may only be 100000 (misc) or 000000
!       (branch).  A "C0" byte would put 1100 at bits 24-27, making
!       the literals 101100 and 001100, which are not legal values
!       of that field at all.  No other statement produces the rest
!       of either half word.
!   (b) A LANDED, ORACLE-VERIFIED SECOND READING of the same
!       instruction: printed p.120 line 2 is "215635.00  217372.10
!       00   B,S DISP" -- the same B with the same 00.
!   (c) line 28's own octal field prints ".1C" for ".10", so this
!       row demonstrably drops ink on round glyphs two characters
!       before it reaches the byte.
! That is the "settle the byte on what produced it" rule, not a
! transcription bent to please the assembler: the STATEMENTS are
! what the page prints, and they were not changed.

!SYM   KSTORE   215710.00
!SYM   SFAKEI   215721.40
!SYM   KKK      215730.00
!SYM   KDOOL    215732.00
!SYM   KSTACK   215742.00
!SYM   KCOPY    215744.00

!CHECK 215710.00 | 000003.00 80 215230.32 A0 | line 5 K STORE TI,13,$UB,S TLR
!CHECK 215711.00 | 000020.00 80 215245.00 A0 | line 6 TI,0,$0,S TLR+13.0
!CHECK 215712.00 | 215231.47 A0 | line 7 BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101 (printed form, assembles as printed)
!CHECK 215712.40 | 215713.07 C6 | line 8 BOPZ,$.32
!CHECK 215713.00 | 215226.11 80 005000.20 50 | line 9 L(BU,5),SPSIOI+.9
!CHECK 215714.00 | 215240.11 80 005000.16 F0 | line 10 CM0111(BU,5),STLR+8.9
!CHECK 215715.00 | 215226.22 00 | line 11 Z,SPSIOI (byte prints open C0; see note)
!CHECK 215715.40 | 215716.05 46 | line 12 BUKZ,$+.32
!CHECK 215716.00 | 215716.45 C6 | line 13 BEEZ,$+.32
!CHECK 215716.40 | 215717.06 44 | line 14 BZEOPZ,$+.32
!CHECK 215717.00 | 215717.46 C6 | line 15 BCSZ,$.32
!CHECK 215717.40 | 000005.34 30 | line 16 LV,14,$CA
!CHECK 215720.00 | 000005.24 30 | line 17 LV,10,$CA
!CHECK 215720.40 | 000032.24 B0 | line 18 V+,10,$10 (printed $1C; $10 = X10 = word 0o32)
!CHECK 215721.00 | 215002.24 B0 | line 19 V+,10,S CHAN S
!CHECK 215721.40 | 000000.64 8A 004066.60 50 | line 20 S FAKE I L(BU,4),S EQUIP($10),-19
!CHECK 215722.40 | 000010.10 30 | line 21 LV,4,$L
!CHECK 215723.00 | 000000.33 8A 216050.34 00 | line 22 BZB,S MULTI($10),K SINGL
!CHECK 215724.00 | 215240.11 80 004071.60 50 | line 23 L(BU,4),S TLR+8.9,-13
!CHECK 215725.00 | 216054.34 C2 | line 24 BRZ,K SIGNL
!CHECK 215725.40 | 000010.16 50 | line 25 LC,7,$L
!CHECK 215726.00 | 215240.15 80 215730.34 00 | line 26 BZB,S TLR+8.13,$+2.
!CHECK 215727.00 | 216272.40 80 | line 27 SIC,K ST CS (fixed KSTCS at 216272.40, not .00)
!CHECK 215727.40 | 216267.10 00 | line 28 B,K CS IN (byte prints open C0; see note)
!CHECK 215730.00 | 000000.70 8A 003067.20 50 | line 29 K KK L(BU,3),S UNIT($10),-18
!CHECK 215731.00 | 000000.26 3A | line 30 LV,11,S UN A($10)
!CHECK 215731.40 | 000010.26 B0 | line 31 V+,11,$L
!CHECK 215732.00 | 000000.30 3B | line 32 K DOOL LV,12,S UN A($11)
!CHECK 215732.40 | 000003.32 3C | line 33 LV,13,S FI A AC($12)
!CHECK 215733.00 | 000000.37 8B 216314.74 06 | line 34 BBZ,S SET UP($11),K RELAY (fixed KRELAY at 216314.40)
